        </p>

        <h2>2. Problem Statement</h2>
        <p>
            Current assistive technologies often function in isolation. A user may have a motorized wheelchair, but that device does not communicate with the smart home environment or the public transit infrastructure. This lack of connectivity creates "friction points" that limit independence and social integration.
        </p>

